<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    WP-K (LSP feasibility validation, dotnet-port\docs\21-lsp-feasibility.md step 1): builds
    VsIntegration\Nemerle.Compiler.Utils (the VS2010 IDE engine, ~22K lines, "Nemerle.Completion2.Engine"
    core) with the core (net10) toolchain, on top of dist\ncc, EXCLUDING the WinForms/CodeDom-designer
    files that are irrelevant to a headless engine (debug AST browser forms, VS Forms-designer
    CodeDom round-trip). Source files are referenced in place under VsIntegration\Nemerle.Compiler.Utils
    (NOT copied) so this project and the legacy VS-targeting Nemerle.Compiler.Utils.csproj/.nproj share
    one source of truth.

    Excluded (WinForms/System.Drawing designer-only; not on the IIdeEngine->LSP surface in
    dotnet-port\docs\21-lsp-feasibility.md), all genuinely coupled to System.Windows.Forms/
    System.Drawing (not just System.CodeDom, see the note further down for that distinction):
      AstBrowserForm.n, Nemerle.Completion2\CompiledUnitAstBrowser.n (debug AST tree Form),
      Nemerle.Completion2\CodeModel\Project.Debug.n (only caller of CompiledUnitAstBrowser; its own
        caller in Project.Relocation.n was already commented out upstream),
      CodeDom\CodeDomHelper.n / FormCodeDomGenerator.n / FormCodeDomParser.n /
        NemerleCodeDomProvider.n / NemerleCodeParser.n / NemerleCodeParserBase.n (the WinForms
        designer round-trip feature cluster: generates System.Drawing.Point-tagged CodeDom members
        for the Forms designer's InitializeComponent() merge),
      Nemerle.Completion2\Engine\BackgroundWorks\Engine-CreateCodeCompileUnit.n /
        Engine-MergeCodeCompileUnit.n (the actual IIdeEngine.CreateCodeCompileUnit/
        MergeCodeCompileUnit bodies, which construct a FormCodeDomParser from the excluded cluster
        above).
    IEngine.n itself is UNCHANGED (shared with the legacy VS build): Nemerle.VisualStudio's Forms
    designer (Project\NemerleFileNodeCodeDomProvider.cs) calls CreateCodeCompileUnit/
    MergeCodeCompileUnit/BeginMergeCodeCompileUnit through the IIdeEngine interface type, so
    removing them from the interface would break that legacy project's compile even though this
    headless build never calls them. Their signatures only reference System.CodeDom types
    (CreateCodeCompileUnitAsyncRequest/FormChanges/MergeCodeCompileUnitAsyncRequest, defined in
    FormChanges.n/CreateCodeCompileUnitAsyncRequest.n/MergeCodeCompileUnitAsyncRequest.n), which
    have no WinForms dependency at all, so those three files ARE included here (see the ItemGroup
    below) together with a System.CodeDom PackageReference (not part of ncc's CoreCLR auto-ref
    set), and CodeDomStubs.n supplies NotSupportedException bodies for the three interface members
    so Engine still fully implements IIdeEngine. A single stray `using System.Windows.Forms;` with
    no actual Forms usage was also dropped from Nemerle.Completion2\CodeFormatting\Formatter.n.

    Build: dotnet build dotnet-port\LspFeasibility\Nemerle.Compiler.Utils\Nemerle.Compiler.Utils.nproj
    (requires dotnet-port\dist\ncc to already exist: run dotnet-port\pack-tool.ps1 first if not).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
    <UseAppHost>false</UseAppHost>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
